From 5c5da79599eafb85bd57126ddd0da45c335c813f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:25:05 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] P5a: IPPingDiagnostics and
 TraceRouteDiagnostics, 22 parameters

Ported from functions/tr098/ipping_diagnostic and traceroute_diagnostic.
The measuring stays in the shell launchers (ipping_launch,
traceroute_launch), queued by DiagnosticsState=Requested exactly as before;
they report with "ubus call tr069 inform" 8 DIAGNOSTICS COMPLETE, which
icwmpd serves.

dm098/diag_mtk.[ch]: what every shell diagnostic shares -- a private
"uci -P <dir>" store per diagnostic, the stop/reset/store tail of every
setter, the Requested launcher, the host check.

dmmtk: mtk_state()/mtk_state_set() (uci -P <dir>, a fresh context per
call so /var/state deltas never leak into /var/state/traceroute),
mtk_kill_cmdline() (pgrep -f | kill -9), mtk_netdev_exists(),
mtk_ere_match().

Queued background commands no longer share icwmpd's stdio:
  - mtk_run_apply_service() read the queue's output to EOF, so a queued
    "launcher run &" held the end of the session until the test finished;
  - the compat script ran the queue with its own stdin/stdout, which are
    icwmpd's request/reply pipe for the coprocess's whole life.

Vendor quirks kept and documented in the files: IPPing Interface stops
the NSLOOKUP diagnostic (copy-paste slip), maps WANIPConnection to a
hard-coded eth0.1; TraceRoute Interface takes a device name; RouteHops.
is always empty (its browse lived in functions/tr181/, never installed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
